  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-11T00:24:06.489Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the past, there used to be more options in the 'Blocks & Mutes' management section of the VRC website. Why they removed these options I have no clue, but there was one that was VERY important to me.\n\nTo try keep this short, my internet connection and VRC don't get along well. If I load more than 2 avatars at a time, the vrchat servers will decide that I don't meet their standards for internet quality and serve me a timeout error (despite still seeing and hearing everyone fine and the downloads coming through fine). \n\nTo get around this, I have EVERY avatar hidden by default via safety settings and manually, one by one, show my friends when I join a world.\n\nThe issue here is that, at the end of a long weekend, I now have a lot of people manually shown. If I join on these friends later and more than 2 of them are shown and wearing a new avatar, I will time out again. I need to re-hide their avatars to not time out.\n\nI used to be able to mass-revoke the 'show avatar' flag using vrchat's website, but it has been removed for a number of months now, leaving me to manually hunt down every person I saw that weekend in-game to reset their avatar status from 'shown' to 'use default (hidden)'.\n\nPlease return the button you removed to the vrc website.",
